  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nThe cooling trend will continue through Wednesday with high\ntemperatures on Wednesday as much as 4 to 8 degrees below average\nfor the mountains and inland valleys. For the coast and valleys, \nhigh temperatures will range from the lower 60s for the far inland\nvalleys to the upper 60s for coastal areas.\n\nChances for measurable rainfall will remain below 10 percent\nthrough Sunday, then increase to around 50 percent from the coast\nto the mountains for Sunday night through Monday, but with the \nchance for 0.25 inch or more only 15 to 25 percent.\n\nChances for rainfall and heavier rainfall will increase\nsignificantly for Tuesday and Wednesday as a strong Pacific storm\nmoves inland into California with the chance of 1 inch or more of\nrainfall from the coast to the mountains for Tuesday morning\nthrough Wednesday night of 75 to 85 percent. The chance for 3 \ninches or more of rainfall ranges from less than 10 percent near \nthe coast to as high as 35 to 45 percent in the mountains of San \nBernardino County.\n\nThe latest model track and timing would bring the most significant\nimpacts into southwestern California for late Tuesday and Tuesday \nnight. Those impacts would also include strong winds and a chance \nof thunderstorms over the coastal waters into coastal areas.",
